<GuidePage
  title="Do I Have Enough Fabric for These Quilt Cuts?"
  description="Use measured rectangles and exact placement geometry to answer fit—not a misleading area total."
  eyebrow="Common Workflow"
  guideSlug="do-i-have-enough-fabric"
  guideCategory="workflow"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Measure usable geometry</h2><p>
      Record each physical stock piece separately with across-fabric width and
      lengthwise length. Total square inches or centimetres cannot prove that
      the required rectangles fit.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Enter every required cut</h2><p>
      Assign each group to the correct fabric and preserve direction, rotation,
      orientation, and WOF-strip constraints. A geometric fit that violates
      grain or motif direction is not valid.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Read the status and unallocated pieces</h2><p>
      No additional purchase means all entered cuts fit the stock. If not, Buy
      now gives the rounded shortfall and the purchased layout accounts for the
      unmet instances.
    </p>
  </section>
  <p>
    For one stock rectangle and one repeated piece, use <a
      href="/calculators/pieces-from-fabric/">Pieces from Fabric</a
    >.
  </p>
</GuidePage>
